# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Raw data — third-party GIS datasets, not committed (see data/README.md)
data/raw/

# Run records and the cell cache — machine-generated, per-developer, and the
# raw-LLM blocks make them large. benchmarks/baselines/ IS tracked; these are not.
data/runs/
data/cache/
# Sweep manifests and their merged cell sets. Same reasoning as run records —
# machine-generated and per-developer — and a swept corridor's cells file runs
# to megabytes of evidence strings.
data/sweeps/

# Derived spatial stores, built from data/raw/ by scripts/build_*.py. Large
# (the geology store is a substantial fraction of the 218 MB source), fully
# reproducible, and machine-generated — so rebuilt, never committed. Everything
# that reads them degrades when they are absent, which is the state on a fresh
# clone. data/reference/ IS tracked: those extracts are small and are what the
# map serves.
data/derived/

# Imported field pins. Somebody's own field notes and GPS positions of workings
# they walked to — not ours to publish, and the "not in any database" set is
# genuinely sensitive.
data/user_sites/
# but keep the README and any human-curated docs we put in data/
!data/README.md

# Source literature — scanned PDFs / archives of published reports.
# Not committed: ~177 MB, redistributable from the original publishers, and
# only the derived markdown in docs/intake_analyses/ is source-of-truth.
# See "Source literature archive" in data/README.md.
FOR GITHUB*.zip
data/literature/
# docs/USGS_assessment_methodology.pdf is deliberately tracked (1 MB, cited by
# docs/04 and the intake analyses). Any other large PDF belongs in
# data/literature/, not in git.

# ArcGIS / ESRI scratch + lock files
*.sr.lock
*.gdb.lock

# Personal working notes — scratch, not documentation.
steps for raghav*.md
